<p>Ehh, this scip is nothing more than a tool for detecting other scips. Though I don't really have an issue with the idea that all anomalous phenomena can apparently be detected by a single entity, this piece does nothing more than straightforwardly lay out the concept. It develops fairly predictably and doesn't even attempt to explore any implications of using the animals. SCP-2000 is more interesting in that there is an attempt at exploring the mystery of the facility's existence, plus the whole idea is just depressing (and executed in such a way). This didn't elicit any emotional or intellectual response from me, frankly. The idea itself just seems so mundane.</p>

